        "passages": [
          {
            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Fagopyrum cymosum, also known as perennial buckwheat or tall buckwheat', is a domesticated plant used in traditional Chinese medicine, for animal feed, and as an ornamental plant. It is native to much of China, and to Bhutan, Nepal, India, Burma, and Vietnam."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p2",
            "text": "Chemistry\nThe flowers are known for their high content of fagopyrin, a naphthodianthrone that provokes phototoxic effects known as fagopyrism."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
